<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84527" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολίχνη</span></b> , ἡ, 
			Dim. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fort, small town,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				41
			</span></i>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, etc.; in earlier writers only as pr. n., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πολίχνη,</span>
			
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πολίχνᾱ,</span> a city in Chios, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.26
			</span></i>; in Ionia, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.14
			</span></i>, etc.; in the Megarid, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.557
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πολιχνῖται</span></b> , οἱ, inhabitants
			of a city in Crete, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.170
			</span></i>.</div>
